# Architecture

Local code-change board (not deployments/runtime ops). Talks to forges via CLIs on the machine.

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| GitHub | `gh` |
| GitLab | `glab` |
| Auth | Existing CLI login sessions |
| AI triage | Optional OpenAI-compatible chat in config `llm` |
| Agent sessions | `strop/agentsession` (prune investigate) via published module |
| Supervision | process-compose (`make serve`); `gitboard serve` for one-off |

## Packages

```
cmd/gitboard/           # CLI: init, sync, serve
internal/config/        # XDG config load/save
internal/cliexec/       # shared gh/glab/git exec
internal/board/         # shared JSON data types (DTOs) for dashboard UI and forge adapters
internal/remotegit/     # GitHub + GitLab adapters (uses board for shared types)
internal/localgit/      # checkouts, worktrees, pull ff-only
internal/syncproj/      # discover + select tracked projects
internal/dashboard/     # aggregate rows for UI; Service (read) and Commands (write) types
internal/server/        # HTTP + static UI
internal/server/static/ # dashboard assets
internal/triage/        # AI failure triage
internal/llm/           # OpenAI-compatible client
internal/pruneagent/    # investigate removable branches
internal/observability/ # OTEL hooks
```

**Dependency direction:** `cmd` → `internal/*`; domain packages must not import `cmd`. Prefer `cliexec` for process calls. Do not grow business logic in `main` switch arms beyond flag parse + wire-up.

## strop dependency

`go.mod` requires the published module (`github.com/behaviorengineering/strop vX.Y.Z`). No git submodule.

**Bump a release:** `go get github.com/behaviorengineering/strop@vX.Y.Z` then `go mod tidy`.

**Local strop changes (rare):** develop in a sibling clone, temporarily add it to root `go.work`, then release strop and bump the require. Do not commit a long-lived `replace` or re-add a submodule unless the user asks.

```
# sibling layout example
use (
	.
	../strop
)
```

After the strop PR/tag lands: remove the sibling `use` line (keep `go.work` with `.` only), `go get …@vX.Y.Z`, `go mod tidy`.

## Dashboard behavior

- Branches column: remote heads from the forge (up to 20); default + open PR/MR first, then by recency. Each row has its own latest CI. CI-only refs do not invent branch rows. Empty `ui.hide_branches` shows all; `path.Match` patterns hide matching names from the board only (forge prune data unchanged).
- Local status beside each remote branch (checked out, dirty, ↑/↓ vs origin). Ahead/behind uses `git fetch --prune origin` (TTL: `local.fetch_seconds`, default 120; `?fresh=1` bypasses) then compares local heads to `origin/<branch>`. Behind + clean → **pull** is ff-only (`git pull --ff-only`, or `git fetch origin branch:branch` when not checked out). Each local appearance (checkout/submodule) with behind-only + clean also gets its own pull control; pulls start immediately (no confirm) and may run in parallel. **Safe prune** on the main worktree fast-forwards the default branch from origin before switching onto it and deleting the merged branch. Worktrees with no remote head are “local only”. Detached HEAD that matches a tag exactly shows the tag name (SHA in tooltip), not only `detached <sha>`.
- `gitboard sync` writes config; a running `serve` reloads the full config file when its mtime advances and clears the forge + origin-fetch TTL caches when the tracked project set changes (no restart required for add/remove or `ui.hide_branches` edits).

## HTTP API

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | Liveness |
| `GET` | `/api/meta` | Server meta |
| `GET` | `/api/dashboard` | Aggregated rows (`?fresh=1` forces refresh) |
| `GET` | `/api/failures?project=&run_id=` | Failed jobs |
| `POST` | `/api/triage` | AI log analysis |
| `POST` | `/api/prune/safe` | Re-check hints; remove a safe local checkout |
| `POST` | `/api/pull/ff` | Fast-forward local branch from origin (ff-only) |
| `POST` | `/api/agents/prune/investigate` | Likely-removable branch evidence + session card |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id` | Session meta, card, turns |
| `GET` | `/api/agents/sessions/:id/failure` | Failure dump when present |

